GeneralsX: FSR 2 reactive mask for particles and other alpha-blended
effects, which leave no depth or motion and smear in the temporal
history. The game sets render state 251 when its opaque scene is drawn;
the D3D9 device copies render target 0 there, and at present FSR 2's
ffxFsr2ContextGenerateReactiveMask compares that copy with the scene
colour of render state 252. DXVK_FSR2_REACTIVE_SCALE (default 0.9, 0 is
off) and DXVK_FSR2_REACTIVE_THRESHOLD (default 0.05) tune the mask,
DXVK_FSR2_SHARPNESS sharpens the scene with RCAS instead of the swap
chain's FSR 1.0 RCAS, and DXVK_FSR2_DEBUG=reactive shows the mask. The
SPIR-V reflection of the FSR 2 passes now leaves out resources a pass
never reads, which the backend would otherwise bind empty.

Output-size traffic, which dominates on integrated GPUs: the upscaled and
composited images are 10-bit UNORM where the device can store and filter
it (16-bit float otherwise), the composite pass applies the RCAS of
DXVK_FSR2_SHARPNESS itself (same mapping as FSR 2) instead of FSR 2's own
RCAS pass, and it reads the EASU image only where the interface is.
DXVK_FSR_TIMING=1 logs the GPU time of each pass every 300 frames.

